From 7397f164ed7b7b2e02a11bf3e887624ca3b86700 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@Averys-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:32:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 34/63] MetalSharp: METALSHARP_TRACE=sync reports the fences
 waited on when no Present comes

A game that stops before its first frame, or between two, is usually waiting on a fence value nothing will
signal. With sync tracing on, a watchdog thread writes, after 5 s without a Present and every 15 s of the same
stall, each fence a thread or a queue waits on: its value, the values waited for and for how long, the GPU
signals queued for it, and the queues blocked on a Wait whose Signal has not been submitted
(VKD3D-Proton-MacOS#11).
