parameters in the top-level argument buffer, which the bridge never provided (and the SM 6.6 heap addresses sat
in its place): converted shaders sampled with a default sampler, which always reads mip level 0 (explicit
levels and pixel shaders' implicit ones alike). Each bridge root signature now gets a table of its static
samplers, whose address is pushed there; the heap addresses follow it.

MoltenVK emulates logic operations and conservative rasterization in SPIR-V-converted shaders, which a converted
