A null acceleration-structure SRV is given the null RTAS's address (vkd3d_get_null_rtas_va) so ray queries through
it traverse a valid, empty structure, but the raw-VA store wrote the descriptor's own Location (0) instead,
discarding it: a ray query on a null descriptor read address 0 (a GPU page fault on MoltenVK).

Metal Shader Converter's modules have no binding for acceleration structures, so a shader that runs ray queries
traverses nothing valid there (the GPU stalls). Graphics and compute pipelines whose SPIR-V declares RayQueryKHR
keep VKD3D-Proton's SPIR-V, whose ray queries use the device's acceleration structures.

"Using resource/sampler tables in root signature, but no heap is bound?" is logged once: games that bind tables
before a heap logged it every frame.
