From 219d4f7e003030d46c4c8cc7b91407af1b3185c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 02:33:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 44/63] MetalSharp: typed buffers, depth-only passes and
 dual-source blending on Metal Shader Converter

Typed buffers: the converter reads a typed buffer through its texel view, from element 0 and as wide as the view,
ignoring the descriptor's element offset. Metal texel views start at any multiple of the texel size (4 bytes for R32,
16 for RGBA32), so the bridge's shadow entry for every buffer SRV and typed UAV now gets a view of exactly the D3D12
view, cached with the resource's other views. PSOs whose shaders use typed buffers go to the bridge; only shaders that
declare a three-component 32-bit typed SRV (no Metal texel format) stay on SPIR-V
(VKD3D_SHADER_META_FLAG_USES_THREE_COMPONENT_TYPED_SRV, which replaces USES_TYPED_BUFFER).

Graphics PSOs of a vertex shader alone (shadow and depth prepasses) go to the bridge, as do PSOs with dual-source
blending: blob version 3 adds a flags word, and VKD3D_MSC_BLOB_FLAG_DUAL_SOURCE_BLENDING has MoltenVK convert the
pixel shader with dual-source blending.
