From 5be004917945a48bde09fb9ddba0f9c15d929ca9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:14:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 48/63] MetalSharp: PSOs that may sample with min/max filtering
 stay on SPIR-V

Metal has sampler reduction only on Apple10 GPUs with macOS 26; elsewhere (M1 to M4) MoltenVK emulates min/max filtering
in SPIR-V shaders, which converted shaders can't do: they read such samplers as linear ones. PSOs whose root signature
has a static sampler with min/max reduction stay on SPIR-V, and, once the application has made such a sampler, so do
PSOs made after that which sample from tables or the heap.
