Views of exactly a D3D12 typed view were kept in their resource's view map, which keeps every view until the resource
goes: views at ever new offsets (ring buffers) grew it without end (tests/perf typed_view_churn: 2.3 GB after 400
frames of 5000 views). A shadow entry now holds a reference to its view: the resource's own when its view map has that
range, otherwise one made for the entry alone, released when the entry is written again, copied over or its heap
goes (192 MB, as SPIR-V's 179). Copies take references.
