From eac55893c5b69bb9bb70427c0eccb812fbd7f019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 05:04:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 51/63] MetalSharp: bridge view lifetimes, DXBC return types,
 and review fixes

- A shadow entry no longer takes a reference to its resource's own view: vkd3d_view_map_destroy frees those
  whatever their count, so an entry outliving its resource freed one again. Such views live as the resource's
  descriptors' do.
- Views made for entries alone are on their resource's list (device->msc.views_mutex): destroying the resource
  destroys their Vulkan views, so a released buffer's memory isn't kept by stale entries; the entries keep the empty
  objects until written again.
- DXBC RDEF return types: D3D_RETURN_TYPE_SINT is 3, UINT 4, FLOAT 5 (Buffer<uint3> was missed, SNORM caught).
- The SHDR/SHEX walk stops at a length past the chunk.
- The bridge's last push is forgotten with the rest of the state (d3d12_command_list_invalidate_all_state): a new
  Vulkan command buffer has no push constants.
