From 81e09e27a32fcf1af59c67085db07d46009a6e93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:18:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 53/63] vkd3d: hoist predication patching again after the
 predicate is written

Without conditional rendering, every predicated draw and dispatch is
patched by a compute shader. After an INDIRECT_ARGUMENT barrier
(PREDICATION is the same state: a predicate the list just wrote, the
usual ResolveQueryData pattern) that patching can't be hoisted, and each
predicated draw ended the render pass around its patch. On MoltenVK that
is a Metal render and compute encoder per draw: 2000 predicated draws
took about 50 ms of CPU and 65 ms of GPU time.

SetPredication now starts a new command buffer sequence when that
happens, as ExecuteIndirect does for state templates: the new sequence's
patch command buffer runs after everything recorded so far. The same
draws take about 0.5 ms of CPU and 0.9 ms of GPU time.
