From 854bb592faa5e78bab11c03fde9681c72fbd3052 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:18:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 54/63] msc: views and samplers made after a bridge PSO switch
 it to SPIR-V

A typed buffer SRV of three 32-bit components reads zeros through the
Metal Shader Converter (Metal has no texel format for it), and a min/max
sampler on a GPU without sampler reduction samples as linear. PSOs made
after the application's first such view or sampler weren't bridged, but
earlier ones were, and read them wrongly.

Bridge PSOs now record whether their shaders read 32-bit typed buffer
SRVs (dxil-spirv's report, or the DXBC reflection; new msc_flags in
vkd3d_shader_meta, cache blob version 5) and whether they sample from
tables or the heap. Once the device has seen such a view or sampler,
their draws and dispatches use the PSO's SPIR-V pipeline, as
ExecuteIndirect state templates already do. PSOs made afterwards with
typed buffer SRVs aren't bridged.
