ExecuteIndirect with a state template writes root arguments in
VKD3D-Proton's layout, so bridge PSOs use their SPIR-V pipeline for it,
which was compiled on the first such ExecuteIndirect: a hitch during
rendering, PSO by PSO. A command signature with a state template now
marks its root signature, and bridge PSOs of a marked root signature
compile that pipeline when they are made (engines create command
signatures at startup, before their PSOs).
