From 8fa674f05fc1fcf66d17e5ba218dc16de214367a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:47:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 57/63] msc: depth bounds PSOs take the bridge where Metal has
 the test

Metal has a depth bounds test on Apple10 GPUs with macOS 26, which
MoltenVK uses; elsewhere it emulates the test in the fragment shader and
refuses bridge pipelines with it. PSOs with the depth bounds test were
kept on SPIR-V everywhere. They now try the bridge, and the first refusal
keeps later ones on SPIR-V without trying (as Mullion picks native or
emulated depth bounds by GPU).
