From 91da49cc4c8af74fb3b84ce0db6cfe9faca0d30d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:54:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 58/63] vkd3d: defer global UAV barriers in render passes too

On MoltenVK, a UAV barrier in a render pass whose pipeline uses no UAVs is
deferred to the end of the pass or the first draw that uses UAVs, so the
pass stays open. Global UAV barriers (no resource named) ended the pass,
since they cover acceleration structures, but those are built outside
render passes: with no build pending, they defer like the others, as
Mullion keeps a pass open across any UAV barrier while it draws without
UAVs. 300 such barriers between draws: 6.3 ms of CPU and 6.7 ms of GPU
time per frame before, 0.10 and 0.26 ms after.
---
