Metal (and so MoltenVK) has no R10G10B10A2_UINT vertex format, and pipelines using
it failed. Where the device can't fetch it, bind the attribute as R32_UINT and pass
its location to the shader compiler (vkd3d_shader_interface_info::
vertex_input_packed_rgb10a2_uint_mask), which unpacks the word. The format now
reports IA_VERTEX_BUFFER support. Such pipelines stay off the Metal Shader
Converter bridge. The input layout formats are part of the pipeline cache key
already.
