From 4979261545369901ac062a6fab5f8d0d5a1ebbf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:21:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 60/63] MetalSharp: sampler LOD bias on the bridge without
 Metal's, min/max samplers on it with

Metal samplers have a LOD bias and min/max reduction only on Apple10 GPUs with
macOS 26 (VK_KHR_portability_subset samplerMipLodBias, which MoltenVK sets exactly
there). Elsewhere MipLODBias was ignored on every path.

- Sampler descriptor entries (heap and static) carry the bias in their metadata,
  as IRDescriptorTableSetSampler writes it; MoltenVK has the converter add it
  (IRCompatibilityFlagSamplerLODBias) to Sample, SampleLevel, SampleBias.
- The converter doesn't add it to gradient samples: shaders with SampleGrad
  (dxil-spirv's new samples_with_gradients, msc meta flag) stay on SPIR-V where a
  biased static sampler, or once a biased heap sampler exists, can reach them;
  bridge PSOs made before then draw and dispatch with their SPIR-V pipeline.
- Where Metal samplers reduce natively, min/max samplers no longer keep PSOs off
  the bridge.

Shader cache blob version 6 (the meta reports gradient samples).
