From a41aa5ac49027b13debe943a46fb3c916e9e78b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:40:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 61/63] MetalSharp: ResourceMinLODClamp on the bridge

The converter clamps samples to the texture entry's metadata
(IRCompatibilityFlagTextureMinLODClamp), counted from the view's first mip:
write the clamp minus MostDetailedMip. It doesn't clamp SampleLevel, so shaders
with explicit LOD samples (dxil-spirv's samples_with_explicit_lod) use SPIR-V once
the application has made a clamped view; bridge PSOs made before then draw and
dispatch with their SPIR-V pipeline.

Shader cache blob version 7.
